      "text": [
        " لاِبْنِهِ أَوْ لاِبْنَتِهِ بِأَبِي أَنْتَ وَ أُمِّي أَوْ بِأَبَوَيَّ أَنْتَ أَ تَرَى بِذَلِكَ بَأْساً فَقَالَ «إِنْ كَانَ أَبَوَاهُ حَيَّيْنِ فَأَرَى ذَلِكَ عُقُوقاً وَ إِنْ كَانَ قَدْ مَاتَا فَلاَ بَأْسَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.564 - Abu Al-Hasan Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as) was asked about a man who says to his son or daughter, \"May my father and mother (or my parents) be ransomed for you.\"\nThe Imam responded: \"If his parents are alive, I consider this to be an act of disobedience (toward them). If they have passed away, then there is no problem.\""
        ]
      }
